From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:24:09 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] Preview tools: drag along a path; snapshot images in
 click coordinates; cursor follows a scaled tab

- preview_drag takes a path of viewport points (with button and modifiers) as
  real mouse input, besides element onto element, so agents can draw on a
  canvas. The panel's cursor follows the path.
- Snapshots read the viewport and pixel ratio from the page instead of the
  headless render scale, so the image is one pixel per CSS pixel (the
  coordinates the click tools take) for desktop tabs too, and report the
  viewport's CSS size.
- Plutonium tabs publish where the page sits in the panel and its scale, so
  the agent's cursor lands on the page after preview_resize.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
